# @seazn/engine is `npm:@onryde/seazn-engine` on GitHub Packages (plan S2-1 Task 1). Only the scope's registry is
# here. The token is never in the repo, and pnpm 10.34.5 ignores an `${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}` credential in a project
# .npmrc ("environment variables are not expanded in registry credentials that come from a project .npmrc"):
# a cold install with that line here was refused 401. The credential line goes in a user-level config instead:
#   local, once: pnpm config set '//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken' '${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}'
#                then NODE_AUTH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token) pnpm install
#   CI: actions/setup-node's `registry-url` and `scope` write it (.github/workflows/*.yml)
@onryde:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
